---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import F from "../data/facts.json";
import EarnCalc from "../components/EarnCalc.astro";
import SceneHead from "../components/SceneHead.astro";
---
<Base title="Earn from idle devices: amader.cloud" description="Rent out the spare storage and computing on your old laptop, desktop or TV box through amader.cloud. How it works, what it pays, and how your files stay private." ogDescription="Store encrypted copies for other members and earn credit, or donate devices you no longer need. What hosting asks of you, and what it pays.">
<section class="page-head photo">
<SceneHead id="towers" />
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Rent out what your devices aren't using.</h1>
    <p class="bn" lang="bn">আমাদের মেঘ, আমাদের হাতে</p>
    <p class="lede">An old laptop is idle most of the day, and most disks are half empty. Through amader.cloud, members rent that spare computing and storage to people who need it, and earn credit off their plan. Later, they'll be paid by bKash.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-bulb" href="contact.html?topic=host">Join the earn list</a><a class="btn btn-line" href="./#earn">Estimate your earnings</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap stack">
  <div class="bp earn earn-embed"><div class="earn-inner wrap-in"><div><span class="kicker">Estimate</span><h2>What could yours earn?</h2><p class="lede">Choose your devices, how long they sit idle, and how much disk you can spare.</p></div><EarnCalc /></div></div>
  <div>
    <h2>Two things you can rent</h2>
    <ul class="ledger">
      <li><div class="fig"><svg class="pict" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-pieces"/></svg>Storage<small>available in the pilot</small></div><div><p>Spare disk space holds encrypted backup copies for other members. You earn <strong>Tk {F.rates.storageTkPer250GB} per 250 GB per month</strong> while your device stays online {F.rates.uptimeTarget} of the time. You can't read what you store, and nobody can tell whose it is.</p></div></li>
      <li><div class="fig"><svg class="pict" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-sandbox"/></svg>Computing<small>starting in 2028</small></div><div><p>Your laptop or desktop runs short computing jobs during the hours you choose: rendering, video conversion, data processing, software builds, and science projects. Our target is <strong>Tk {F.rates.coreHourTk.toFixed(2)} per core-hour</strong>. A 4-core laptop idle 10 hours a day would make about {F.economics.laptopEarn} a month, minus roughly {F.economics.laptopPower} of electricity. Final rates depend on demand.</p></div></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <h2>Who rents it</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>University and research groups in Bangladesh with batch jobs that don't need a data centre</li>
        <li>Local startups: media conversion, data processing, software builds and test runs</li>
        <li>Other members, whose backups need copies in more than one place</li>
        <li>Volunteer science projects, so idle hours are never wasted</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small" style="margin-top:14px">Buyers pay about {F.economics.buyerCoreHour} per core-hour. That undercuts the cheapest small cloud servers in the region, which cost about {F.economics.cloudCoreHour} per processor-hour. We pass most of that to the member, and keep a share to run the service.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>How we keep your device yours</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Jobs run in a sealed sandbox, a separate virtual machine with no access to your files, accounts or home network.</li>
        <li>The sandbox only talks to our job server. Nobody can browse the web, send email or hide traffic through your connection.</li>
        <li>You set the hours. Jobs pause when you open the lid, and a laptop's battery never drops below 80%.</li>
        <li>We check every job before it runs, and we refuse crypto mining, scraping and anything the acceptable use policy forbids.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel-dusk">
    <h2>What it asks of you</h2>
    <div class="promises">
      <div><svg class="pict" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-server"/></svg><h3>A device we manage</h3><p>Any laptop, desktop or TV box on one of our plans. We set up the sandbox and keep it updated.</p></div>
      <div><svg class="pict" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-bell"/></svg><h3>Power and a wire</h3><p>Plugged in and on your router's cable. For storage, it should stay online through load-shedding, which in practice means a mini UPS.</p></div>
      <div><svg class="pict" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-coins"/></svg><h3>Nothing else</h3><p>We match jobs, check results, and send you a monthly statement of hours, storage and credit.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <svg class="pict" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-school"/></svg><h2>For schools: labs that fund themselves</h2>
      <p>Pathshala lab laptops can rent out their computing after school hours. The credit pays towards the lab's monthly plan, so donated devices keep earning for the school that uses them.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-line" href="contact.html?topic=school">Ask about a lab</a></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <svg class="pict" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-hand"/></svg><h2>Only want to donate?</h2>
      <p>If your building has three or more devices to give away, we collect them for free. We reset phones in front of you, and send a wipe record for every computer. We rebuild the working ones for schools and community projects, and send the rest to a formal recycler.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-line" href="contact.html?topic=donate">Arrange a collection</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
